   "source": [
    "Goal: Identify words preferred by one author over another by comparing word frequencies.\n",
    "\n",
    "Approach:\n",
    "\n",
    "Data: Collect multiple plain-text works by each author. Clean them by removing punctuation and standardizing case.\n",
    "\n",
    "Focus: Analyze function words they reveal unconscious stylistic habits regardless of topic.\n",
    "\n",
    "Method:\n",
    "\n",
    "Tokenize texts and count relative word frequencies.\n",
    "\n",
    "Build a Document-Term Matrix (rows = texts, columns = words, values = frequencies).\n",
    "\n",
    "Use Burrows's Delta to measure stylistic distance between texts (smaller Delta = more similar style).\n",
    "\n",
    "Use Zeta to identify marker words—those consistently frequent in one author and rare in the other.\n",
    "\n",
    "Tools: Python\n",
    "\n",
    "Outcome: Words with high Zeta scores for Author A vs. Author B are the preferred words that distinguish their styles.\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
